_ZN9hpp_proto22shift_mix_parse_varintIjLi4ETkNS_8concepts21contiguous_byte_rangeENS_13pb_serializer19input_buffer_regionISt4byteEEEEDTclL_ZNSt3__16ranges5__cpo5cdataEEfp_EERKT1_Rl:
  123|  8.65M|    -> decltype(std::ranges::cdata(input)) {
  124|       |  // The algorithm relies on sign extension for each byte to set all high bits
  125|       |  // when the varint continues. It also relies on asserting all of the lower
  126|       |  // bits for each successive byte read. This allows the result to be aggregated
  127|       |  // using a bitwise AND. For example:
  128|       |  //
  129|       |  //          8       1          64     57 ... 24     17  16      9  8       1
  130|       |  // ptr[0] = 1aaa aaaa ; res1 = 1111 1111 ... 1111 1111  1111 1111  1aaa aaaa
